WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.860
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.380
Велком-то привет, русский!

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.940
Эпе соот 58, it's 13 июля 2026 года.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.800
I'm Olia, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:11.340
Ready?

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.040
Поехали.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.640
That means let's go.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.540
Today's word of the day is sabaka.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:17.700
So baka.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.900
Say it with me slowly.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:20.580
So baka.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.420
Now faster, sabaka.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.380
It means dog.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.740
Imagine a Siberian husky barking so baka,

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.440
like it's calling its own name.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.020
My sabaka loves to run.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.420
That means my dog loves to run.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:33.800
Now you try it.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.320
Repeat after me, sabaka.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.320
Let's build more animal words together.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.640
Our first new word is mid-veh.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.720
Mid-veh, namazgid-katka, is kmitis-kustikov.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.740
Дальше вы можете грумон-крест, минч-кран-бер.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.560
Think of my head, what I've yet growled at the end.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.060
Like a bear, what a big head.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.260
Repeat after me.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.280
Mid-veh.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.180
Большой, mid-veh, pit-vlesoon.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:57.520
That sentence means the big bear sleeps in the forest.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.140
Next comes птица.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.080
Птица, птица means bird.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:04.060
Птица fleets, like a tweet from a tiny bird.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.180
Repeat after me.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.460
Птица, птица, поет на дереве.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.180
The bird sings in the tree.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.980
Now, рыба, рыб пойдет на стратку.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.540
Рыба, раим с вытрифер, а фиш in the reef.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.660
Repeat after me.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.840
Рыба, рыба плавает в воде.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.460
The fish swims in the water.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.860
Лошадь из next, рушадь, лошадь means horse.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.280
Лошадь sounds like low-shad where a horse might hide.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:28.580
Repeat after me.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.440
Лошадь, лошадь, бежит быстро.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.040
The horse runs fast.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.100
Remember, мышь from before.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.320
It's still means mouse.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.640
Мышь, маленькая мышь, есть сыр.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.200
The little mouse eats cheese.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:40.980
Кот comes after.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:41.500
Кот.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.100
Кот means tonkiet or milk-ket.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.320
Кот is short and cozy, like a cat crawled up.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.640
Repeat after me.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:49.220
Кот.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:53.020
Кот сидит на окне, the cat sits on the window.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.640
Заяц is our last new word today.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.160
Заяц, заяц means hair or rabbit.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.960
Заяц sounds like заяц, racing across a field.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.060
Repeat after me.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.740
Заяц, заяц прыгает в поле.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.340
The hair jumps in the field.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.740
Russian nouns have gender that change the words around them.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.340
Most animal names ending in a consonant like kot are masculine.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.860
Words like pizza and the river are feminine.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.880
In English, we rarely mark gender on nouns.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.200
In Russian, you say a big cat for big tomcat.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.680
But a big pizza for big bird.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.800
Now you can say, my cat for my cat in the masculine form.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.340
Or my river for my fish in the feminine form.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.820
That small change makes your sentences sound natural.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.020
In Russian fairy tales, animals often act like wise teachers

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.320
or tricky helpers.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.460
The bear is strong, but kind, the fox is clever.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.200
The wolf can be both scary and funny.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.640
Kids grow up hearing stories like the bear and the fox.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.100
Those tales teach lessons through animal adventures in snowy forests.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.040
Draw your favorite animal from today's list.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:08.040
Label it with the Russian word, then roar, bark or chirp the word three times.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:10.860
For adults, look at a pet photo or zoo picture.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.680
Say three full sentences using today's words.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.180
Try it a sabaka, она бежит.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.660
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.060
Midwet and the English idea of honey-eater are secretly cousins.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.200
This word started in ancient Slavic roots.

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.760
Mewd meant honey.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.380
Vedat meant to know.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.520
So midwet literally means the one who knows honey.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.300
It was a polite way to avoid seeing the real bear name in angering the animal.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.440
The word traveled through old Slavic languages.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.400
It never borrowed from Latin Ursus like most European tanks.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.320
Both cultures used sweet nicknakes to talk about the scary forest giant.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.420
Next time you see honey, remember it is cousins with midwet,

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.600
молодец, that means well done.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.080
Remember, every expert started as a beginner, practicing today's words out loud,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.220
even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.420
See you next time, пока, that's Russian for buy.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:14.380
And if you'd rather watch then listen, find us on YouTube at www.mirroru.links in the show notes.

